## The agent's verbs

`sdt` is broad; this page is the part an agent uses. For the rest, read
`sdt schema` or `context/sdtdocs/`.

- `sdt context new|path|list --type <t>` — create a work file ({{.NewTypes}}), print
  its path ({{.PathTypes}}), list one kind ({{.ListTypes}})
- `sdt read -p <file|corpus-ref> [--section] [--lines a:b|-N:] [--numbered]`,
  `context edit <doc> [--append]` — one reader with line numbers and a real
  `--format json`, and a body writer that appends or replaces
- `sdt context get|set|unset <doc> [<key>] [<value>]` — a frontmatter key, bytes
  preserved; `status`/`updated` are CLI-owned
- `sdt context status get|set|vocab|sync`, `deprecate|rename|rm` — lifecycle; a
  terminal status plus `--reason` closes
- `sdt context task add`, `sdt context check <doc> [id] --state done|wip|block` —
  checklists (`--phase`/`--all`/`--grep`); never ticked by hand
- `sdt context search`, `list` — the query engine
- `sdt context relations parent|similar|rank|path` — parent, neighbours,
  ranked candidates, chain
- `sdt context reindex`, `lint` — index, corpus
- `sdt context budget` — the always-loaded surface; informational, never a gate
- `sdt grep [-A/-B/-C] [--path <file>]`, `find [glob]`, `ls [--stat] [--depth]`,
  `edit -p <f> --old/--new`, `diff <a> <b>`, `write -p <file>`, `sdt q` for
  JSON — the working tree, bounded
- `sdt agent doctor|verify|gate|refresh` — health, instruction contract, the
  project's `gate:` steps, a re-render

## Search before asking

A question the corpus answers is answered **from the corpus**: search before
asking what a document says; when the corpus cannot answer, say so, naming the
paths you read. It holds after a compaction, too.

## Output discipline

A verb is an interface to a budget:

- **Cap what a verb prints**: truncate, filter, or pipe `--format json` into
  `sdt q`; a large result becomes a `context/tmp/` file and the line naming it.
- **Batch what can be batched**: one command over several beats several; a
  repeated identical invocation is a missing flag.
- **Read the tiered index once**, then open only what it points at. A short result
  prints in full: nothing is capped for a rule's sake.

## Context queries

`list` and `search` share one conjunctive engine returning the same set. Dates:
`--after`/`--before` (aliases `--since`/`--until`), `--last <N><unit>` (`m` `h` `d`
`w`), `--date created|updated`, as `YYYY-MM-DD`, RFC3339 or `now[±N<unit>]`.
Fields: `--type`, `--status`, repeatable `--where <key>=<value>` (or `!=`) over any
frontmatter field — a list matches a member, an absent key never matches `=`.

Logging, exit codes, global flags: `context/instructions/reference.md`.
